    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0160" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/114<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >3/12</hi>a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Nicholson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-04T15:00:00-04:00">August 4, 1940—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Department’s circular telegram July 11, 4 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d187-f1"
                    /> The War Department has designated Major L. Mathewson, U. S. Army, and the
                    Navy Department has designated Major C. C. Jerome, U. S. Marine Corps, and
                    Captain F. L. Riefkohl, U. S. Navy, to conduct <pb facs="0161" n="149"
                        xml:id="pg149"/> the proposed staff conversations with the Nicaraguan
                    officials. It is expected that they will arrive in Managua in time for the
                    conversations to begin August 26. You will be informed through the Legation at
                    San José of the proposed date and means of their arrival in Managua. Following
                    the conclusion of their conversations in Managua Majors Mathewson and Jerome
                    will proceed to Honduras and Captain Riefkohl will return to the Canal Zone.</p>
                <p>A separate telegram<anchor n="7" xml:id="d187-f2"/> is being sent you outlining
                    are agenda for the proposed conversations, which you may communicate in
                    strictest confidence to the appropriate Nicaraguan authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
